 "chunks": [
  {
   "scene": 1,
   "start": 0.12,
   "end": 4.643,
   "text": "In 2000, Blockbuster had the chance to buy Netflix for fifty million dollars."
  },
  {
   "scene": 1,
   "start": 4.923,
   "end": 5.669,
   "text": "It said no."
  },
  {
   "scene": 2,
   "start": 6.369,
   "end": 8.631,
   "text": "Back then, Blockbuster was the king of movie night."
  },
  {
   "scene": 2,
   "start": 8.911,
   "end": 14.415,
   "text": "Thousands of stores. And in 2000, nearly eight hundred million dollars from late fees alone."
  },
  {
   "scene": 3,
   "start": 15.115,
   "end": 19.36,
   "text": "Netflix started in 1997, renting DVDs by mail."
  },
  {
   "scene": 3,
   "start": 19.64,
   "end": 23.395,
   "text": "Its founders, Reed Hastings and Marc Randolph, were losing money fast."
  },
  {
   "scene": 4,
   "start": 24.095,
   "end": 28.425,
   "text": "So they flew to Dallas, and offered to sell Netflix to Blockbuster for fifty million."
  },
  {
   "scene": 4,
   "start": 28.705,
   "end": 31.009,
   "text": "Blockbuster's boss, John Antioco, said no."
  },
  {
   "scene": 4,
   "start": 31.289,
   "end": 33.316,
   "text": "Randolph says he was struggling not to laugh."
  },
  {
   "scene": 5,
   "start": 34.016,
   "end": 36.917,
   "text": "Netflix kept growing. A monthly plan. No late fees."
  },
  {
   "scene": 5,
   "start": 37.197,
   "end": 38.968,
   "text": "Then, in 2007, streaming."
  },
  {
   "scene": 6,
   "start": 39.668,
   "end": 43.529,
   "text": "Blockbuster peaked in 2004, with over nine thousand stores."
  },
  {
   "scene": 6,
   "start": 43.809,
   "end": 48.14,
   "text": "But customers moved online, and in 2010, Blockbuster went bankrupt."
  },
  {
   "scene": 7,
   "start": 48.84,
   "end": 51.187,
   "text": "Today, Netflix is worth hundreds of billions."
  },
  {
   "scene": 7,
   "start": 51.467,
   "end": 54.112,
   "text": "And just one Blockbuster is left, in Bend, Oregon."
  },
  {
   "scene": 7,
   "start": 54.392,
   "end": 55.459,
   "text": "Be kind. Rewind."
  }
 ]
